(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #108 aliasing probe: LANGUAGE.md's own Format Strings
 as Values example carries a format-string text into an `Execute`
 argument list through exactly this shape - `append tok to cmdargs` is a
 retaining read (a list append), so `tok`'s later `Set` must not free the
 string `cmdargs` still holds an element pointer to. `/bin/echo` prints
 the untouched original value, proving the argv entry survived.)

a number called n is 5.
a text called tok is "{n}".
a list called cmdargs is [].
append tok to cmdargs.
Set tok to "changed".
Execute "/bin/echo" with arguments cmdargs.
